 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2017-09-12",
   "text": "Medicare Buy-In and Health Care Stabilization Act of 2017\n This bill makes a series of changes relating to health insurance options and costs. Among other things, the bill establishes a Medicare buy-in option for individuals aged 50 to 64, requires the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services to negotiate drug prices for Medicare beneficiaries, and establishes an individual market reinsurance fund."
  }
 ],
